From 1ab972e3ccb25c25787204cf5cb9a23a75a9ab99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NikoMalik <NikoMalik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:01:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] crash: keep __crash_kexec out of line

__crash_kexec() is STACK_FRAME_NON_STANDARD because crash_setup_regs()
stores rbp and the other registers from inline asm,but it is only
__noclone,so thinLTO with the raised inline threshold folds it into
crash_kexec() and objtool checks the body there:

  vmlinux.o: warning: objtool: crash_kexec+0x13b: stack state mismatch: reg1[5]=-1+0 reg2[5]=-2-160

mark it noinline so the annotation covers the code it was written for,
it runs once on panic so the call costs nothing
---
 kernel/crash_core.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/crash_core.c b/kernel/crash_core.c
index 4f21fc3b108b..fa6b1e2692ab 100644
--- a/kernel/crash_core.c
+++ b/kernel/crash_core.c
@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@ static void crash_cma_clear_pending_dma(void)
  * only when panic_cpu holds the current CPU number; this is the only CPU
  * which processes crash_kexec routines.
  */
-void __noclone __crash_kexec(struct pt_regs *regs)
+void __noclone noinline __crash_kexec(struct pt_regs *regs)
 {
 	/* Take the kexec_lock here to prevent sys_kexec_load
 	 * running on one cpu from replacing the crash kernel
-- 
2.56.1

